invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide_edwards.h
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: select_entry tests the mask and moves on when the entry is not
  the digit's, so the scan keeps one entry of eight, and which one is
  three bits of the private key on the control path. The values stay
  right, so the vectors, the equivalence binary and the proofs all pass;
  only the count of what the compiler emits sees it: x25519_wide.c rises
  above its ceiling on both 64-bit specs.

--- old
        uint64_t mask = equal_mask(size, j + 1);
        word_pair masks = {mask, mask};
--- new
        uint64_t mask = equal_mask(size, j + 1);
        if (mask == 0) {
            continue;
        }
        word_pair masks = {mask, mask};
